Aerie-Purpose: Scale canvas measureText metrics by a factor from a new per-site text-metrics token, stable for a site in a session, and turn it on; rekey the off-by-default client rect noise the same way (issue #118).
Aerie-Upstream-Area: third_party/blink/renderer/modules/canvas/canvas2d/base_rendering_context_2d.cc (measureText), third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/document.cc and document.h (GetNoiseFactorX, GetNoiseFactorY), third_party/blink/renderer/core/helium_noise/text_metrics_noise.cc, third_party/blink/public/common/helium_noise/ (HeliumNoiseFeature::kTextMetrics), content/browser/helium_noise/noise_token_data.cc, third_party/blink/common/features.cc (kHeliumNoiseTextMetrics), chrome/browser/bromite_flag_entries.h
Aerie-Kind: hook

Amends helium-chromium/patches/bromite/fingerprinting-flags-client-rects-and-measuretext.patch. That
patch scales measureText and the client rects by a factor from base::RandDouble(), drawn once per
Document, so every load of every page got another factor. A tracker can read two loads of one site, or
two sites, and a value that changes on every load is itself a fingerprint of the protection. It also
stayed off behind a flag.

HeliumNoiseFeature::kTextMetrics is a new surface token, added the way hardening/0010 adds kWebGL and
hardening/0015 adds kScreen: a session token in HeliumNoiseTokenData that GetTokens derives per site
(hardening/0011), and a renderer that receives it only when protection is on for the site. "Token
present" therefore means "protected here", and the global switch and the per-site switch give the real
metrics back without a renderer change. Workers get the token with the other tokens (hardening/0013,
0014), so measureText on an OffscreenCanvas in a worker follows its site as well. The new feature
kHeliumNoiseTextMetrics (on by default) switches the surface off for the Bench's negative control.

The factor is 1 plus or minus 0.00015% (the range of the Bromite patch), taken from one of 2^20 steps
that the site's token hashes to. The range, the step list and the decision are pure code with unit tests
in overlay/components/aerie_text_metrics. One Blink function, TextMetricsNoiseFactor in
core/helium_noise, reads the feature switches and the token and does the hashing. Each kind of value
(measureText, client rects x, client rects y) hashes the token with its own number. measureText
now scales every metric by the factor without the Bromite runtime flag, which no longer changes it; the
flag entry says so. The client rect noise keeps its flag and stays off by default, and now reads the
same kind of factor, 1 without a token. Nothing else about layout changes: the noise touches only the
values a script reads, and a layout fixture in the Bench (a sticky header and a virtual list) shows it.

This patch also removes what the Bromite patch added to the Document constructor, the two Document
members and the base/rand_util.h include, because nothing draws a random factor any more.

